+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Redemption persistence (repositories)
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `src/repositories/couponRedemptionRepository.ts` with a `redeem({ orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, createdAt })` method that runs BEGIN → update the order's `discount_cents`/`final_amount_cents`/`coupon_code` → insert a `coupon_redemptions` row → increment `coupons.used_count` → COMMIT, rolling back on any error. Add a `findByOrderId(orderId)` read. Verify with a test that `redeem` updates all three tables and that `findByOrderId` returns the inserted row.
+- [x] 1.2 Verify atomicity: a test that forces the redemption to fail (e.g. a foreign-key/constraint violation) leaves the order fields, `coupon_redemptions`, and `coupons.used_count` unchanged.
+
+## 2. Coupon application rules (service)
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Implement `CouponService.applyToOrder(orderId, rawCouponCode)` with the documented error precedence: body validation (`INVALID_REQUEST`), order existence (`ORDER_NOT_FOUND`), order status (`ORDER_NOT_PENDING`), already-applied (`COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`), coupon lookup on the trimmed/uppercased code (`COUPON_NOT_FOUND`), status (`COUPON_INACTIVE`), validity window from the injected `Clock` (`COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`/`COUPON_EXPIRED`), usage limit (`COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED`), minimum amount (`MINIMUM_NOT_MET`); on success call `redeem` and return the reloaded order. Verify with tests for each rejection code and for the precedence of overlapping conditions.
+- [ ] 2.2 Implement the discount math (base by `FIXED`/`PERCENT` with `Math.floor`, apply non-null `maxDiscountCents` cap, clamp to `amountCents`, `finalAmountCents = amountCents - discount`) and check it against every acceptance example (AC-01…AC-05). Verify with tests asserting `discountCents`/`finalAmountCents` for each case.
+- [ ] 2.3 Update `src/app.ts` to construct the redemption repository and pass the new `CouponService` dependencies (`coupons`, `orders`, `redemptions`, `clock`). Verify `npm run build` passes and existing tests still pass.
+
+## 3. Route (HTTP layer)
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, parsing the id with `parseId` and forwarding the raw `couponCode` to `coupons.applyToOrder`; update `registerOrderRoutes` and its call in `app.ts` accordingly. Verify an end-to-end `app.request` test returns HTTP 200 with the updated order for a valid request.
+- [ ] 3.2 Add route-level tests covering the full response shape (identical to `GET /orders/:id`, including the normalized uppercase `couponCode`), the `" save20 "` normalization case (AC-10), the second-application `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` case with unchanged amounts (AC-08), and the redemption side effects (AC-09: `usedCount` +1 and a new `coupon_redemptions` row).
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [ ] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and confirm the whole suite (existing tests plus the new ones) passes.
+- [ ] 4.2 Re-read `specs/coupon-redemption/spec.md` against the implemented behavior and confirm each scenario and error-table row is covered by a passing test or a deliberate, documented gap.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change with `/opsx:archive` once review requirements are satisfied.
+- Verify the archived result updates `openspec/specs/coupon-redemption/spec.md`.
